Z||000000||Fiero STS||12-28-2001||10:04 PM||||need any help on wiring for northstar conversion I am using 98 engine. have talked with Howell and find their harness incomplete and not sure how much of the senders and controls will have to be switched. checked on holley controller and found out it wont run transmission. also there are issues with Speedometer and tach am I forgetting anything ? any help will be appreciated. I want to be sure what I buy will work before I spend money and find out I need to spend more and more and more to get it to work or find out there is something better out there.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Will||12-28-2001||10:47 PM||||DIY.<BR>If you want it done right, do it yourself.<P>We've hybridized the wiring harnesses from a automatic V6 Fiero with the harness from a '95 Northstar. All the information necessary is in the factory service manuals (~$130 for Cadillac, ~$80 for Fiero).<BR>It looks like we will have 35-40 man hours in the harness, but it will look as though the factory put it there.<BR>We're using a Getrag, BTW.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||12-28-2001||11:30 PM||||If you're using the auto, just mod the Caddy harness.  Should be easy enough.<P>If you're using a manual tranny, get <A HREF="http://www.chrfab.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.chrfab.com</A>   's modified Holley 950.  It comes complete with harness all ready for you.<P>Go with aftermarket AutoMeter gauges.  Junk the old fiero stuff.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Jay||12-29-2001||12:08 AM||||Ditto<P>I found Howells harness lacking.  No wirring for the Caddy ICP and connectors that were completely wrong.  Do it yourself.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
